<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Khanate of Khoy</h1><p class="st-meta">1747 CE – 1799 CE (approx.) · capital Khoy</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A khanate of the Kurdish Donboli family in north-western Iran whose last khan resisted the Qajars and ended his days ruling a khanate under Russia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Donboli, a Kurdish family long settled around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoy">Khoy</a>, held hereditary authority there under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah's</a> death in 1747 they ruled Khoy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salmas">Salmas</a> as a khanate. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-khan-donboli">Ahmad Khan Donboli</a> (r. 1763 to 1786) was the most powerful of the line, extending his influence over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoy">Khoy</a> lay on the main route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and the Ottoman frontier and was a prosperous trading town. The Donboli khans kept tribal cavalry and patronised building in the town. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-khan-donboli">Ahmad Khan</a> was murdered in 1786, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jafar-qoli-khan-donboli">Jafar Qoli Khan Donboli</a> opposed the rising power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agha-mohammad-khan-qajar">Agha Mohammad Khan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agha-mohammad-khan-qajar">Agha Mohammad Khan</a>'s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran</a> took control of the region in the 1790s; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jafar-qoli-khan-donboli">Jafar Qoli Khan</a> fled north in 1799 and was later installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> as khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaki-azerbaijan">Sheki</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoy">Khoy</a> became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1747 CE – 1799 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.47%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1747 CE – 1799 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Khoy</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmad Khan Donboli, Jafar Qoli Khan Donboli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Azerbaijani Turkic, Kurdish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khoy Khanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1773&amp;focus=khanate-of-khoy" aria-label="Khanate of Khoy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5797 794 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khanate of Khoy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6117 1050L6298 1144M6117 1050L6364 1269"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6298 1144h0M6364 1269h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6117 1050h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6117 1050h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Khoy. <a href="/atlas?year=1773&amp;focus=khanate-of-khoy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

